tion if strong fundamentals resurface and market conditions improve.  Reflecting on past mistakes, I recognize that overly optimistic biases can lead to premature entries or holding through declines. This reinforces the importance of balancing bullish narratives with tangible risks, especially in volatile or uncertain environments. Prioritizing caution and data-driven decision-making enhances our chances of avoiding unnecessary losses and positioning ourselves for more favorable entries in the future.  In summary, given the weight and validity of risks highlighted by the bear, I recommend holding at this time, with strategic management steps to safeguard the portfolio.
